I once threw together a very small program to parse save files and
print out the sizes (and optionally locations) of the various branches
of the dungeon.  My reason was that a character had died on Quest-5 (when
the Quest was 6 levels deep), and it was getting annoying trying to get
more characters of the same level as far as the Quest only to discover
that the bones wouldn't load because the level didn't exist.

(Last time I updated [s], I spent ages getting the bones files off the
system - I couldn't bear to lose them.  Is this obsessive compulsive
disorder?)

It was a single file that needed to be compiled from inside the nethack
source tree, with the same config options as were used to compile
NH itself.  It was an absolutely abominable hack, and *just* worked
under gcc (native Linux and MinGW cross-compile), but if anyone's
actually interested, I could try and clean it up to make it portable
enough that others can use it.  Alternatively, if there's a better
solution already out there, I'd like to know - it'll save me sanding
down the rough edges on this wheel I'm reinventing. :-)

